<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kouris River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kouris is one of the main rivers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, rising in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troodos-mountains">Troodos Mountains</a> and flowing south to the sea near Episkopi, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limassol">Limassol</a>. Ancient Kourion stood on the cliffs near its mouth and ruled the fertile land along its valley. The Kouris Dam, completed in 1988, holds the island's largest reservoir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kouris-river.jpg" alt="Kouris River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shell from Limassol, Cyprus · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kouris_River_-_off_to_sea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
